          %h2#the_connection_to_natural_homotopy The connection to natural homotopy
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sierpinski+topos"} Sierpinski topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Set
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^2
            is a connected, locally connected and local topos. As a result of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Artin+gluing"} Artin gluing
            along
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Set
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi id
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set\overset{id}{\to}Set
            it has two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point+of+a+topos"} topos points
            (corresponding to the two points of the underlying
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sierpinski+space"} Sierpinski space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Set
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^2
            as an abstract
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interval+object"} interval object
            for a homotopy theory of Grothendieck toposes correlated with their nature as “generalized spaces” and view, accordingly, the exponential
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Set
                        %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}^{Set^2}
            as a path space for
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
          %p
            (Cf. Beke
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#B00"} 2000
